We need to produce a final solution that works. The issue is that when a keyboard-only user types a date and presses Enter, the flatpickr's onMonthChange/onYearChange handlers reset the date to the first available day of the month (due to applyUnavailableDates). The verifier's evidence shows that after typing the date, the date field is changed to the first day of the month (01/11/2026) instead of the typed date (02/11/2026). This happens because the onMonthChange handler is triggered when the date changes (maybe due to flatpickr internally adjusting the month?). Actually, the user typed a date in the same month (October? Wait: they typed 02/11/2026 which is November 2, 2026). The initial date is set to today (maybe October 26, 2026). When they type 02/11/2026, the month changes from October to November, triggering onMonthChange, which then calls getUnavailableDates and then applyUnavailableDates with setDate=true, which sets the date to the first available day in that month (which is the 1st). So we need to prevent the onMonthChange/onYearChange from causing a date reset when the change is due to manual entry.

Our approach: add a flag manualDateEntry set on keypress Enter, and in onMonthChange/onYearChange, if flag is true, skip the getUnavailableDates call and reset flag.

But we also need to ensure that the date change event still triggers getAvailableHours (via onChange). That's fine because onChange is called before onMonthChange? Actually flatpickr's onChange triggers when the date changes, and onMonthChange triggers when the displayed month changes. In our case, typing a date that changes the month will trigger both onChange and onMonthChange. We want onChange to proceed (to update available hours) but we want to prevent onMonthChange from resetting the date.

Thus we set manualDateEntry=true on keypress Enter, then in onMonthChange/onYearChange, if manualDateEntry is true, we skip the getUnavailableDates call and reset the flag.

We also need to ensure that the flag is reset after skipping.

